WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.350
Speaker 1: All right.

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:04.600
So next part of this incredible story, part
one is Trump under criminal investigation.

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.269
Part two, a number of statements from the
attorney general, Merrick Garland, over the

00:00:08.269 --> 00:00:14.190
last week or ten days indicating a willingness,
at least theoretically, to prosecute a former

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.190
president.

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:16.190
Okay.

00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:17.190
We have been waiting for these signals.

00:00:17.190 --> 00:00:19.160
The first signal is the following.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:22.080
Here is an interview with Lester Holt that
Merrick Garland did yesterday.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.260
Speaker 3: You said it in no uncertain terms
the other day that no one is above the law.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:34.769
That said, the indictment of a former president
of the perhaps candidate for president would

00:00:34.769 --> 00:00:37.100
arguably tear the country apart.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:40.379
Is that your concern as you make your decision
down the road here?

00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:42.289
Speaker 1: I really hope that's not as concerned.

00:00:42.289 --> 00:00:45.179
Speaker 3: Or do you have to think about things
like that?

00:00:45.179 --> 00:00:50.100
Look, we pursue justice without fear or favor.

00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:57.609
We intend to hold everyone, anyone who was
criminally responsible for the events surrounding

00:00:57.609 --> 00:01:03.889
January six or any attempt to interfere with
the lawful transfer of power from one administration

00:01:03.889 --> 00:01:05.829
to another, accountable.

00:01:05.829 --> 00:01:07.119
That's what we do.

00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:11.820
We don't pay any attention to other issues
with respect to that.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:15.700
So if Donald Trump were to become a candidate
for president again, that would not change

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:19.590
your schedule or how you move forward or don't
move forward.

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:26.750
I'll say again that we will hold accountable
anyone who was criminally responsible for

00:01:26.750 --> 00:01:31.430
attempting to interfere with the transfer
or legitimate lawful transfer of power from

00:01:31.430 --> 00:01:33.040
one administration to the next.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:36.390
Speaker 1: So that is quite clear from Merrick
Garland.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.390
That is quite clear.

00:01:37.390 --> 00:01:40.800
And there has been an increased, increasingly
noticeable shift in this direction.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:46.409
Now, on July 20th, this was about a week ago,
Merrick Garland also made very clear, and

00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:47.930
that's the statement that was referenced.

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:52.350
No person is above the law, also believed
to be a signal about what may be coming.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:55.720
Speaker 3: We are entering as only.

00:01:55.720 --> 00:02:02.659
Later if there are charges brought against
a former president related to January six.

00:02:02.659 --> 00:02:06.109
DOJ could be accused of playing politics.

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:08.090
How is the department?

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.960
How are you waiting for that?

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:16.530
Also, do you think that there is a constitutional
question here about whether you charge former

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:20.040
president for actions allegedly taken during
his term?

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:21.350
Separately, Jalen Walker.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.100
Kaitlin Walker McConnell, answer.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:24.100
Okay.

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.100
Let me answer.

00:02:25.100 --> 00:02:26.100
Okay, look.

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:35.590
No person is above the law in this country.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:36.590
Nothing stops us.

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:37.590
No, I don't know how to say that again.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:38.590
No person is above the law in this country.

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:39.590
I can't say it any more clearly than that.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:49.850
There is nothing in the principles of prosecution
and any other factors which prevent us from

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:59.100
investigating anyone, anyone who's criminally
responsible for or for an attempt to undo

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.620
a democratic election.

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:07.040
Speaker 1: So that was the first signal that
there was something going on.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:12.340
And then, of course, over the last 24 hours,
we have learned Trump under criminal investigation

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:18.220
by the federal government, the Justice Department,
a major, major deal which we will continue

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:19.220
to follow.

00:03:19.220 --> 00:03:24.280
Now, again, I don't want I don't want to be
negative.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:26.270
I don't want to be pessimistic.

00:03:26.270 --> 00:03:31.840
But do I really see charges announced against
Donald Trump by Merrick Garland?

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.870
I don't know that I do.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:35.420
I don't know that I do.

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:37.780
But I will, of course, concede.

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:43.170
I think it is more likely today than at any
point over the last two or three years during

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.870
which I've been asked about it again and again
and again.

